1
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:59,530
Morning, Grandpa.

2
00:01:59,530 --> 00:02:03,530
Is something the matter, Grandpa?

3
00:02:03,530 --> 00:02:14,530
The editorial in this paper has my friend Nat Baker real upset.

4
00:02:14,530 --> 00:02:17,530
Ah! I'll read it to you.

5
00:02:17,530 --> 00:02:22,530
"The old library building on Chestnut Street, “Chestnut

6
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:25,530
which has been vacant for over a year now,

7
00:02:25,530 --> 00:02:28,530
was supposed to be made into a community center

8
00:02:28,530 --> 00:02:30,530
to serve the senior citizens

9
00:02:30,530 --> 00:02:32,530
as well as the younger people of Riverdale.

10
00:02:32,530 --> 00:02:34,530
Due to lack of funds

11
00:02:34,530 --> 00:02:37,530
for the repainting of the interior of the building

12
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:39,530
and for the furniture needed,

13
00:02:39,530 --> 00:02:42,530
the plans for the community center

14
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:45,530
have been postponed indefinitely."

15
00:02:45,530 --> 00:02:49,530
He's coming over to talk about it.

16
00:02:49,530 --> 00:02:51,530
Is it that serious a problem, Grandpa?

17
00:02:51,530 --> 00:02:53,530
It is.

18
00:02:53,530 --> 00:02:57,530
Nat's not as lucky as I am, Robbie. Nat

19
00:02:57,530 --> 00:02:59,530
He doesn't have any family with him.

20
00:02:59,530 --> 00:03:01,530
He lives alone

21
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:05,530
and depends on places like a community center

22
00:03:05,530 --> 00:03:08,530
to be with people--people his own age.

23
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:12,530
But there's the old community center on Elm Street.

24
00:03:12,530 --> 00:03:13,530
It's small,

25
00:03:13,530 --> 00:03:20,530
and the problem is that it's set up primarily for kids to play.

26
00:03:20,530 --> 00:03:26,530
Ping-Pong tables, soda machines, and lots of music.

27
00:03:26,530 --> 00:03:29,530
It's too noisy for some older people like Nat.

28
00:03:29,530 --> 00:03:32,530
I never realized that.

29
00:03:32,530 --> 00:03:36,530
It's hard for some older people to take all that noise.

30
00:03:36,530 --> 00:03:40,530
That's why the new community center is a good idea.

31
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:42,530
Part of the building for older people,

32
00:03:42,530 --> 00:03:44,530
part of the building for younger people.

33
00:03:44,530 --> 00:03:46,530
I see what you mean.

34
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:49,530
That must be Nat.

35
00:03:49,530 --> 00:03:51,530
It could be Alexandra.

36
00:03:51,530 --> 00:03:54,530
She's coming over this morning to help me with my math.

37
00:03:54,530 --> 00:04:02,530
Hi, Robbie.

38
00:04:02,530 --> 00:04:04,530
Hi, Alexandra. Come on in.

39
00:04:04,530 --> 00:04:09,530
Do you want something cold to drink?

40
00:04:09,530 --> 00:04:11,530
I'd love some cola, please.

41
00:04:11,530 --> 00:04:13,530
Cola coming up.

42
00:04:13,530 --> 00:04:17,530
I really appreciate you coming over to help me with my math.

43
00:04:17,530 --> 00:04:19,530
My final exam is next Tuesday.

44
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:22,530
You're so good in all your other subjects.

45
00:04:22,530 --> 00:04:24,530
I just can't understand

46
00:04:24,530 --> 00:04:26,530
why you have so many problems with math.

47
00:04:26,530 --> 00:04:28,530
Hi, Alexandra.

48
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:29,530
Hi, Mr. Stewart.

49
00:04:29,530 --> 00:04:32,530
I thought that was Nat Baker who rang the front doorbell.

50
00:04:32,530 --> 00:04:35,530
Don't let me interrupt you.

51
00:04:35,530 --> 00:04:36,530
No problem, Grandpa.

52
00:04:36,530 --> 00:04:37,530
We're just having some cola

53
00:04:37,530 --> 00:04:40,530
before getting to the tough stuff--math.

54
00:04:40,530 --> 00:04:44,530
He'll do anything to avoid getting down to math lessons,

55
00:04:44,530 --> 00:04:45,530
Mr. Stewart. Stewart

56
00:04:45,530 --> 00:04:48,530
I was the same way.

57
00:04:48,530 --> 00:04:49,530
Really, Grandpa?

58
00:04:49,530 --> 00:04:52,530
Really. I didn't like math.

59
00:04:52,530 --> 00:04:56,530
I wasn't good at it, and I didn't like studying it.

60
00:04:56,530 --> 00:04:58,530
But you had to be good at math.

61
00:04:58,530 --> 00:05:00,530
You graduated from engineering school.

62
00:05:00,530 --> 00:05:03,530
I was. But not in high school.

63
00:05:03,530 --> 00:05:06,530
For some reason, I couldn't get a handle on it.

64
00:05:06,530 --> 00:05:10,530
Then, in college, I became good at it.

65
00:05:10,530 --> 00:05:12,530
Then there's hope for Robbie.

66
00:05:12,530 --> 00:05:13,530
I can't wait.

67
00:05:13,530 --> 00:05:17,530
You think I can just skip it now and get to it at college?

68
00:05:17,530 --> 00:05:20,530
You'll never get to college to find out, Robbie,

69
00:05:20,530 --> 00:05:21,530
if you skip it now.

70
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:24,530
That must be Nat.

71
00:05:24,530 --> 00:05:29,530
Sit down, Robbie. Let's get to work.

72
00:05:29,530 --> 00:05:43,530
I'd like you to meet my friend Nat Baker.

73
00:05:43,530 --> 00:05:47,530
This is Alexandra Pappas, and this is my grandson Robbie,

74
00:05:47,530 --> 00:05:49,530
whom I think you've met once or twice before.

75
00:05:49,530 --> 00:05:51,530
Nice to meet you, Mr. Baker.

76
00:05:51,530 --> 00:05:53,530
Hi, Mr. Baker. We met before.

77
00:05:53,530 --> 00:05:54,530
Where?

78
00:05:54,530 --> 00:05:57,530
In town. At the hardware store.

79
00:05:57,530 --> 00:06:02,530
I remember now. Right. Hi.

80
00:06:02,530 --> 00:06:03,530
Hello, Alexandra.

81
00:06:03,530 --> 00:06:07,530
Don't let us keep you from your math tutoring, Robbie.

82
00:06:07,530 --> 00:06:09,530
I know you want to get to it.

83
00:06:09,530 --> 00:06:10,530
Stay ... stay.

84
00:06:10,530 --> 00:06:14,530
I told you. He'll use any excuse to avoid math.

85
00:06:14,530 --> 00:06:17,530
Did you read the story in the paper, Malcolm?

86
00:06:17,530 --> 00:06:18,530
I did.

87
00:06:18,530 --> 00:06:21,530
It's a serious matter for a lot of us.

88
00:06:21,530 --> 00:06:22,530
A serious matter.

89
00:06:22,530 --> 00:06:24,530
It is. Come on out to the patio.

90
00:06:24,530 --> 00:06:25,530
We'll talk about it out there.

91
00:06:25,530 --> 00:06:28,530
Thanks. Nice to meet you ... again.

92
00:06:28,530 --> 00:06:32,530
What's the problem?

93
00:06:32,530 --> 00:06:35,530
Come on! You'll hear about it.
